# Line endings
#
# The index is already LF throughout, but nothing in the repository enforced
# that — it held only because every commit so far came from a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true. A contributor with autocrlf=false would commit CRLF and
# turn the next diff of that file into a whole-file rewrite. `text=auto` makes
# the normalisation a property of the repository instead of a property of
# whoever happens to be cloning it.
#
# Four files currently sit as mixed-ending in the working tree
# (src/app/api/status/route.ts, src/app/layout.tsx,
# src/components/shared/index.ts, src/styles/admin-store.css); this settles them
# on checkout without changing what is stored.
* text=auto

# Explicit LF for anything a tool or runtime parses, where a stray CR is a bug
# rather than a cosmetic difference.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary

# Collapse the lockfile in GitHub review and keep it out of language stats.
#
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`: that marks the file binary, so `git diff` reports
# only "Bin 277673 -> 277464 bytes" and a dependency change becomes impossible
# to review locally. `linguist-generated` already collapses it in pull requests,
# which is the part worth having.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
